DGR-02: folded graph freed with base value 0 while its arrays are based (heap corruption)
=========================================================================================
Harness: ../common. Same as DGR-01 but with base value 1 (foldfi args: 0 1 5 1 1 1).

Pristine:
  cd ../common; ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/foldfi 4 0 3 6 -- 0 1 5 1 1 1
  nth=3 exit=124 :: HANG (vertex group failed: vertloctax still NULL, nothing misfreed, DGR-01 hang)
  nth=4 exit=134 :: (0): ERROR: dgraphFold2: out of memory (4); fishim: rank 0: signal 6 (glibc abort: free(): invalid pointer)
  nth=5 exit=134 :: (0): ERROR: dgraphFold2: out of memory (5); signal 6
  nth=6 exit=134 :: (0): ERROR: dgraphFold2: out of memory (6); signal 6
  With base 0 the same runs only hang: the wrong-base free is invisible.

Patched: nth=3..6 exit=1 on all ranks, no abort; nth=7 exit=0.
Twin hdgraphFold2() has the identical ordering (memSet at hdgraph_fold.c:182, baseval at :879) and
is fixed in the same commit; exercised through orderfi (see ../DGR-01/README).

Correction (review round 2, 7.0.18, plain -O1 build, np=4, m16x16_b1.grf via orderfi, rank 0):
  pristine 7.0.18 shows SIGSEGV at 2 allocation indices (nth 85 and 86 in that build) and HANG at the fold
  sites (nth 87-93); the earlier "three allocation failures" count is not what a re-run gave. Indices depend
  on the build flags. With the G18 series the fold sites return 1 on all ranks; nth 83/84 (dgraphHaloSync2)
  still hang and nth 85/86 (hdgraphInduceList unchecked memRealloc, PS2-G18-1) are fixed only by series 0163.
